d and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 18 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast biopsy   is a 5 x 4 x 2 7cm oriented lumpectomy specimen  The external surface is lobular tan yellow adipose tissue and has two long stitches marking the medial margins and two short stitches demarcating the lateral margins  The specimen is inked anterior blue  posterior black  superior green  inferior yellow and serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal tan yellow adipose tissue intermixed with tan white fibrous tissue  No discrete masses or lesions are appreciated  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A J from medial to lateral including all inked margins  Resident  STEWART M  KNOEPP  MD   Ph D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan M  Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Unchecked.
