Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    GRADE II III  WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF MARGIN  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPES  PRESENT AT INKED SURFACE  PRESENT ADJACENT TO AND AWAY FROM INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  3  PAPILLOMA  MICROSCOPIC  4  CALCIFICATION WITHIN LOBULES ADJACENT TO CARCINOMA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular invasion is not seen  The intraoperative diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 14                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Specimen received fresh in the Frozen SectiOn Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm mass with an ill defined lobular mass which lies within 0 1cm of several inked surfaces  Representative tissue samples are submitted in cassettes A to F with closest margins in A and B  tumor in C and D and other suspicious areas in E and F  Gross Description by  ANTHONY FORRESTER  HMS Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
