Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 05  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Frozen Section Pathologist  None Frozen Section Resident  None Frozen Section Consultant s   None Consulting Pathologist s   None Assigned Resident Path  Kristina Braaten  M D  Reports To  MICHELE ANNETTE GADD  M D  CLINICAL DATA  ILC with persistent positive margins  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   CAPILLARY HEMANGIOMA  INCIDENTAL  NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and   right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 8cm right simple mastectomy specimen  with a stitch designating 12 o clock  There is an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm white skin ellipse  with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm eccentric everted nipple  2 0cm  superior lateral to the nipple there is a 3 5cm tangental umbilicated scar  which comes to within 0 2cm of the skin margin  The anterior aspect of the breast is inked blue  the posterior black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm cavity  which comes to within 0 5cm of the deep margin and 1 3cm of the scar on the skin surface  The tissue surrounding the cavity is white and fibrotic to tan and glistening to focally yellow and chalky  The tan  glistening comes to within 0 3cm of the deep margin  This cavity and fibrous tissue is central  The remainder of the cut surface consists of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and white rubbery fibrous tissue  No additional lesions or masses are identified  No lymph nodes are appreciated  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to deep margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavity to scar at skin surface   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue adjacent to cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue away from cavity  Gross Dictation by Michael R Tan  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Kristina Braaten M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Kristina Braaten M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT BREAST MASS    EXCISION  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE I III   PRESENT AT AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  LOW GRADE  PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES ALONG A BROAD FRONT AND INVOLVING A RADIAL SCAR   SEE NOTE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  Ductal carcinoma in situ is present in 3 of 10 slides  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 05                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm piece of breast tissue  It is incised and sectioned to reveal breast parenchyma with multiple  focal  rubbery  nodular areas  No frozen section is done  Representative sections are submitted in cassette A through J  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST MASS   NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
