Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 48 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SOLID AND COMEDO TYPE WITH FOCAL MICROINVASION  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  Diagnosis by  Shane Meehan  MD Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 19                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The in situ carcinoma cells stain for estrogen recptor protein  The in stiu carcinoma cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive tumor cells are not present in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fibrofatty tissue fragment with a localizing wire and accompanying x ray  Inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular  firm  white area which corresponds to the areas of calcification noted on x ray  submitted in A and B  and the rest is submitted entirely in C through I  Resident  FANG FANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS  SUSPICIOUS AREAS TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Unchecked.
