Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  05 MAY 93 at 14 48 CLINICAL DATA  None provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  98   WITH EXTENSION INTO SKELETAL MUSCLE WITH CARCINOMA PRESENT AT AN INKED SURGICAL MARGIN   SEE NOTE  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    NOTE  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 93 at 12 29                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   Estradiol receptor  Negative  Progestin receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 28     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  o