Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 28 CLINICAL DATA  An excisional biopsy on REMOVED_DATE showed invasive ductal carcinoma  grade III III with lymphatic invasion and free margins  There was also ductal carcinoma in situ extending to within 0 1cm of one margin  A re excision on REMOVED_DATE showed ductal carcinoma in situ grade III III extending to within 0 4cm of a margin  as well as extensive lymphatic permeation by carcinoma extending to within less than 0 1cm from a margin                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 10 41                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a 1 006 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm simple mastectomy specimen with an irregular contour  A REMOVED_DATE x 9 9cm skin ellipse is attached  with an areola which measures 5 8cm in diameter and a nipple which measures 1 3cm in diameter  There is a 4 9cm linear scar located 5 3cm lateral to the nipple  The overlying skin is otherwise externally unremarkable with no evidence of nipple or skin retraction  Externally  the specimen is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm biopsy cavity which is open and in communication with the deep  posterior  margin  The specimen is inked as follows  black intact deep  posterior  margin  blue superior lateral quadrant  orange  superior medial quadrant  green inferior lateral quadrant  yellow inferior medial quadrant  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal that the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 1cm biopsy cavity extends to within 2 5cm of the anterior margin in the superior lateral quadrant and underlies the linear scar noted on the skin ellipse  Radiating in all directions from the biopsy cavity is irregular  firm  white yellow scar tissue  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow  fibrofatty and unremarkable  It is extensively searched for lymph nodes  and none is identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A B  Biopsy cavity to adjacent deep margin  C F  Biopsy cavity  G  Parenchyma away from biopsy cavity in superior lateral quadrant  H   Lymph node  Resident  JOHN BRANDA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
