Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 11 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  DISPLAYING BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CHARACTERISTICS  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  CARCINOMA IN SITU EXHIBITING BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CHARACTERISTICS  EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The results of immunohistochemical staining for keratin will be reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 59     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR KERATIN LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   THE LYMPH NODES DO NOT CONTAIN KERATIN POSITIVE CARCINOMA CELLS  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 06 52     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and an accompanying specimen radiograph  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal focally yellow focally white breast parenchyma showing focal cystic changes  No discrete lesions are noted  The specimen is submitted in its entirety in cassettes A F  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary nodes  is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which multiple firm lymph nodes are identified ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Representative sections of each lymph node are submitted in cassettes G K  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  NO LESION GROSSLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_I