or cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is an oriented  long stitch lateral  short stitch superior  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fibrofatty breast tissue with a localization needle in place  The specimen is inked  superior red  inferior yellow  posterior black  anterior blue   serially sectioned displaying a fibrofatty focally blue dyed cut surface  The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from lateral to medial in cassettes A M with the lateral and medial en face margins in cassettes A and M respectively  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axillary sentinel lymph node  are 2 tan pink lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  Both lymph nodes are bisected one of which has a faint blue tint  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  N  1 bisected blue tint lymph node  O  1 bisected lymph node  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional superior  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm tan yellow fibrofatty breast tissue with a suture designating farthest from tumor  The specimen is inked  furthest from tumor black  opposing side blue   serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes P W  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right br