Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  07 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 17 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  MULTIPLE FRAGMENTS   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  SEE NOTE   2  ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  TWO FOCI   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  4  PERILOBULAR HEMANGIOMA  5  THE FROZEN SECTION LAB GROSS DIAGNOSES ARE CONFIRMED  NOTE  Invasive tumor is present in the third of four specimens received in the frozen section lab  The tumor extends to within 0 5mm of the inked resection margins  Neither lymphatic nor blood vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm soft fatty tissue of breast  inked and sectioned to reveal a fibrofatty cut surface  No frozen is done  Representative section submitted in cassettes from A J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  right breast  are two fatty soft fragments of breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm respectively  Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibrofatty scarred surface  No frozen is done  Representative sections are submitted from cassettes K T  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a specimen with two pieces  The first one is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and contains a stellate ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan yellow nodule ascending to the margin  Entirely submitted in cassettes from U Z  with a nodule in U  The second fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable cut surface and is entirely submitted from AA CC  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  with the patient s name and unit number is a fourth specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in diameter  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable cut surface  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes DD MM  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     G